concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 Application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The amendments made by items 1 to 5 of this Schedule apply in relation to corrupt conduct, whether engaged in before or after the commencement of the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006. (2) However, the requirement for the Chief Executive Officer of Customs to notify a corruption issue to the Integrity Commissioner under that Act only applies on and after this item commences. (3) To avoid doubt, the amendments made by items 1 to 5 apply in relation to corrupt conduct even if the conduct was engaged in at a time when Customs was known as the Australian Customs Service. (4) In this item: corrupt conduct has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006. corruption issue has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859  Proceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2 Responsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          5" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The amendments made by items 1 to 5 of this Schedule apply in relation to corrupt conduct, whether engaged in before or after the commencement of the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006. (2) However, the requirement for the Chief Executive Officer of Customs to notify a corruption issue to the Integrity Commissioner under that Act only applies on and after this item commences. (3) To avoid doubt, the amendments made by items 1 to 5 apply in relation to corrupt conduct even if the conduct was engaged in at a time when Customs was known as the Australian Customs Service. (4) In this item: corrupt conduct has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006. corruption issue has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859  Proceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2 Responsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          5"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d562b0b47e9b2109524f6621b4711769cf770ce8ef285eb7f8191fc78f8daa61" ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Amendments apply in relation to corrupt conduct, regardless of when it was engaged in." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf> ;
    dc:source "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.8" ;
    cml:asserts concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6-norm .
