concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-196 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "196 At the end of subsection 25A(2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-196 ;
    values:originalText "Add: Note: Under that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see the definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime authority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred between these authorities (see section 315B of that Act). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859  Proceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2 Responsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          31" ;
    skos:definition "Add: Note: Under that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see the definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime authority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred between these authorities (see section 315B of that Act). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859  Proceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2 Responsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          31"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "557be39a5c60b66ef02e561ffc4ee11dfd9c2939c4595854a92c0568f9dbfbd0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines responsible authorities for proceeds of crime" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf> ;
